{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++17 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++17 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nYou are given three positive integers x,\u2009y,\u2009n. Your task is to find the nearest fraction to fraction  whose denominator is no more than n. Formally, you should find such pair of integers a,\u2009b (1\u2009\u2264\u2009b\u2009\u2264\u2009n;\u00a00\u2009\u2264\u2009a) that the value  is as minimal as possible.If there are multiple \"nearest\" fractions, choose the one with the minimum denominator. If there are multiple \"nearest\" fractions with the minimum denominator, choose the one with the minimum numerator.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++17 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <set>\n#include <map>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#include <iomanip>\n#include <queue>\n#include <stack>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <numeric>\n#include <functional>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing ll = long long;\nusing pii = pair<ll, ll>;\nusing vi = vector<ll>;\n\nconst ll MOD = 1000000007;\nconst ll INF = 1000000000000000005LL;\n\ninline ll gcd(ll a, ll b) {\n    return b == 0 ? a : gcd(b, a % b);\n}\n\ninline ll ceil_div(ll a, ll b) {\n    return (a + b - 1) / b;\n}\n\nvoid solve() {\n    ll x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    set<pii> candidates;\n    \n    for (ll i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        ll mini = (x * i) / y;\n        ll maxi = ceil_div(x * i, y);\n        \n        if ((mini + maxi) * y > 2 * x * i) {\n            ll g = gcd(i, mini);\n            candidates.insert({i / g, mini / g});\n        } else {\n            ll g = gcd(i, maxi);\n            candidates.insert({i / g, maxi / g});\n        }\n    }\n    \n    pii best = *candidates.begin();\n    \n    for (const auto& [q, p] : candidates) {\n        ll lhs = p * y;\n        ll rhs = x * q;\n        \n        if (lhs == rhs) {\n            best = {q, p};\n        } else if (lhs > rhs) {\n            if (best.second * y > x * best.first) {\n                if (p * best.first < best.second * q) {\n                    best = {q, p};\n                }\n            } else {\n                if (2 * x * best.first * q > y * (best.second * q + best.first * p)) {\n                    best = {q, p};\n                }\n            }\n        } else {\n            if (best.second * y > x * best.first) {\n                if (2 * x * best.first * q < y * (best.second * q + best.first * p)) {\n                    best = {q, p};\n                }\n            } else {\n                if (p * best.first > best.second * q) {\n                    best = {q, p};\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    ll g = gcd(best.first, best.second);\n    cout << best.second / g << '/' << best.first / g << '\\n';\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    int t = 1;\n    while (t--) solve();\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <set>\n#include <map>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#include <iomanip>\n#include <queue>\n#include <stack>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <numeric>\n#include <functional>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing ll = long long;\nusing pii = pair<ll, ll>;\nusing vi = vector<ll>;\n\nconst ll MOD = 1000000007;\nconst ll INF = 1000000000000000005LL;\n\ninline ll gcd(ll a, ll b) {\n    return b == 0 ? a : gcd(b, a % b);\n}\n\ninline ll ceil_div(ll a, ll b) {\n    return (a + b - 1) / b;\n}\n\nvoid solve() {\n    ll x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    pii best = {0, 1}; // numerator, denominator\n    ll min_diff = LLONG_MAX;\n    \n    for (ll i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        // Find the best numerator for denominator i\n        ll a = (x * i) / y;\n        \n        // Check both floor and ceil\n        vector<ll> candidates = {a};\n        if (a + 1 <= (x * i + y - 1) / y) { // ensure a+1 is valid\n            candidates.push_back(a + 1);\n        }\n        \n        for (ll num : candidates) {\n            // Calculate absolute difference |x/y - num/i| = |x*i - y*num| / (y*i)\n            ll diff_num = abs(x * i - y * num);\n            ll diff_den = y * i;\n            \n            // Compare fractions without floating point: diff1 < diff2 iff diff1_num * diff2_den < diff2_num * diff1_den\n            if (diff_num * best.second < min_diff * diff_den) {\n                min_diff = diff_num;\n                best = {num, i};\n            } else if (diff_num * best.second == min_diff * diff_den) {\n                // Same difference, choose smaller denominator, then smaller numerator\n                if (i < best.second || (i == best.second && num < best.first)) {\n                    best = {num, i};\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Simplify the fraction\n    ll g = gcd(best.first, best.second);\n    cout << best.second / g << '/' << best.first / g << '\\n';\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\